+# FAA alternate operational forms: entries, time labels and unresolved joins
+
+October 30, 2026. **The referenced daily operations and Area B personnel forms are present in the released packet.** Their visible entries give a more specific record trail than the earlier review's references alone. The reviewed supervisor-role candidate has two different recorded time ranges in different tables; the operations-manager candidate has a printed on-duty entry. Neither result authenticates the original personnel statement, clock basis, version chronology or a complete sign-in/sign-out history.
+
+Three candidate Area B handoff pairs show a consistent **four-hour difference between printed labels**. That is conditional field arithmetic, not a measured clock error or an established timezone conversion. All values and earlier claims remain preserved.
+
+## Source and actual scope
+
+Held official source **AEA1130 / NARA 7598367**: [catalogue](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7598367), [exact released PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/4-UAL-175/e-Other/4-AEA-1130-COMPLETED-ACCID-PCKG--FORMAL-ACCID-PCKG-ZNY-ARTCC-148-UAL175-REDACT-SEALED.pdf). Acquired October 30, 2026; **15,505,493 bytes / 237 pages**, SHA-256 `5bb71c00b716fb59425571d0c714a97a32d84b13f35dcc65d7cc6bd6f83b5179`.
+
+No new download occurred. Exactly **16 new page images** were read: **8, 16, 21–33 and 40**. This exhausted the declared cap. Six selected text/header pages received visible-raster OCR after image reading; roster, handwriting and faint-data pages were read manually without unnecessary OCR. Across this source-review series, **34 distinct packet images are known read; 203 have not been examined in these studies**. This is not a claim about what every other investigator has read.
+
+The originals and rasters remain on guarded Intel storage. No hidden PDF text extraction, redaction reconstruction, roster publication, voice/radar processing, decoder test or clock fit occurred. Raw PDFs/rasters/full OCR, names, operating initials, signatures, whole rosters, contact/address/tracking/account and private-case information are excluded from this derivative.
+
+[SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) supplies source/raster/OCR hashes and exact scope; [FORM-CROSSWALK.json](FORM-CROSSWALK.json) records the selected observations and their limits. Table row numbers below count data rows manually from the first row under the column headings; they are not printed source row IDs.
+
+## The actual forms and the earlier review
+
+The comparison source is [AEA1129's released review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0681d662e507d45698521d40dff151ea7d9543af/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-shipping-receipt-originals-2026-10-30/README.md), SHA-256 `226568e667bb9f63dbc9579ea5f8e6b9e8a6dc54856a71eb726d0061c54feaed`. It was already read. Section 6 physical 2 / OCR 14–34 cites alternate forms or unavailable logs; Section 11 physical 4 / OCR 22–44 discusses personnel-statement verification.
+
+| Earlier source statement | Newly read source | What remains unresolved |
+|---|---|---|
+| Operations-manager sign-in/sign-out said to appear on FAA Form 7230-4 | Section 4 divider at physical 21 names the form. Physical 22/23 contain its actual pages 1/2 and 2/2. A candidate on-duty entry has label **1030** on physical 22 / OCR 26. | The candidate association uses the specific form reference, visible unredacted surname/first initial and role context. It is not independently authenticated unique identity. No explicit matched off-duty entry has been established from these two pages. A later **1743** on-duty row for another person is not assigned as this person's off time. |
+| Supervisor on-position information said to appear in Area B personnel log / “3600.1” | Physical 24/25 are Personnel Logs / Area B dividers. Personnel-log pages show the printed identifier **ZNY 3600-1 (REV.9/96)**, including physical 27/28. | The review's dot and the form's hyphen are retained as literal identifier formats. Exact native version/mapping is not authenticated by similar titles alone. |
+| Supervisor said not to have signed the personnel log for the period indicated in a statement; automated sign-on said not required | Physical 28 / printed 3 of 8 / data row 22 contains candidate time labels **0632–1432**. Physical 31 / OSIC/CIC certification / data row 3 contains **0632–0810**. | The original statement and the period it meant have not been read here. Table purpose, clock convention, applicability of the claimed rule and whether this released version was available when reviewed remain open. Neither Time Off value is selected as controlling. |
+| Military-position sign-on log said not to exist; two TMU-role logs said unavailable | Those claims remain in AEA1129. The newly read material is an Area B personnel/operations set. | An Area B form is not automatically the military/TMU record. No absence, destruction, no-duty conclusion or rule compliance is established. Similar surnames or different first initials must not be joined into a claimed match. |
+
+The newly visible entries qualify blanket claims that no relevant staffing record survives. They do not prove that the earlier review was wrong, that all periods are documented or that a particular entry existed at the time of review. Differing purposes, periods, clock conventions, versions, annotations and mistaken associations remain untested possibilities. Native copies and the exact personnel statement are the discriminating inputs.
+
+## Candidate handoff pairs: preserve the labels
+
+| Certification locator | Certification Time On label | Daily operations locator | Daily printed label | Nominal difference |
+|---|---:|---|---:|---:|
+| Physical 31, data row 4 | **0810** | Physical 22 / OCR 34 | **1210** | 240 minutes |
+| Physical 31, data row 5 | **0930** | Physical 22 / OCR 45 | **1330** | 240 minutes |
+| Physical 31, data row 6 | **1315** | Physical 23 / OCR 14 | **1715** | 240 minutes |
+
+These are manual candidate role/event associations from visible fields. Names and operating initials are omitted. The calculation tests the written labels **conditional on the associations being valid**. It does not establish an actual four-hour lag, an error, a universal offset or the dates/timezones of an event.
+
+A differing clock convention is one untested explanation; different event/version associations or transcription issues are other untested possibilities. No source value is converted, corrected, normalized or treated as controlling. Historical timekeeping/form instructions, native headers and the actual statement/clock sources are required before adjudicating those possibilities.
+
+Other cells have crossings or annotations. They were preserved in the images and were not silently read as an authorized final value. The two supervisor-role ranges, **0632–1432** and **0632–0810**, refer to differently titled tables; their difference is not labelled missing or unaccounted time.
+
+## What the operations log actually reports
+
+Physical 22 / OCR 35–39 records these notice/advice statements:
+
+| Printed time label | Source-reported content, paraphrased |
+|---:|---|
+| **1238** | Informed of possible hijack **AAL11** |
+| **1250** | Informed of another possible hijack **UAL175** |
+| **1250** | Advised an aircraft crashed into the World Trade Center |
+| **1304** | Advised a second aircraft crashed into the World Trade Center |
+
+These are **reported notices in an operations log**, not directly measured impact times or independently authenticated moments of awareness. The form's header prints **09/11/01 00:38**; the function of that header clock field has not been established. No creation-time or later edit chronology is inferred.
+
+The source includes more than one aircraft/event. That observation does not resolve the separate AAL11/UAL175 and case-label conflicts in earlier released memoranda. Nor does a 2001 notice row establish what any official knew about an inaccurate May 2003 answer or its later correction.
+
+Physical 22 also contains weather-service computer/wind-data remarks (OCR 14–22) and stated frequency/radar/VOR outage windows (30–31). Those are source-level technical follow-up inputs. No site/feed/channel mapping, actual target or audio coverage loss, outage cause or link to the attacks has been tested. Such work remains with the assigned technical owner.
+
+## Pagination and record-type limits
+
+| Physical page(s) | Actual observed printed label/type |
+|---|---|
+| 26, 27, 28, 29 | Personnel Log **1, 2, 3, 4 of 8** |
+| 30 | Operational Overtime or Additional Personnel; a page counter was not established in the visible scan |
+| 31 | OSIC/CIC Certification, **6 of 8** |
+| 32 | Sign In / Sign Out Correction Form, ZNY Form 7210-5, **7 of 8**; visible entry grid blank |
+| 33 | Swap / Change of Assignment form, **Page 1** |
+
+Eight consecutive physical images do not authenticate a continuous matching 1–8-labelled set. The next observed page after “7 of 8” is a different form labelled “Page 1.” **Page 8 of 8 has not been located within this reading scope**; physical 34 was not examined because the cap was reached. Do not infer deletion, insertion or missing source material from the offsets alone. The blank correction grid does not prove that no correction occurred in other records.
+
+Two additional navigation discoveries remain narrowly qualified:
+
+- **Physical 16 / OCR 3–21:** Boston TRACON's Certified Index, dated September 19, 2001, claims originals were on file: forms 7230-4, 7230-10, 8020-6-1, A90 sign-on log, personnel statements, original voice recordings and certified cassette recordings. This is a source claim about then-current holdings, not seven independently counted objects, present survival or a New York TMU-log inventory.
+- **Physical 40, prominent warning label:** the document is described as derived from computer magnetic recordings/internal processing and not an exact representation of the control-position display. This is a representation qualification. Underlying faint/covered values were not reconstructed; no original-data/display comparison was performed.
+
+The packet's shared case header does not make different facilities, record types, copies or clocks interchangeable.
+
+## Next records and tests
+
+1. Read the **exact reviewed personnel statement** and its period; join it to the visible staffing/certification entries without assuming the tables measure the same activity.
+2. Obtain date-appropriate form/timekeeping and position-sign-on instructions, native versions, correction/approval history and clock-basis records. A signed-looking scan is not native signing or edit-history authentication.
+3. Inspect the next held packet pages in a later bounded unit to determine the actual Section 5/6 boundary and whether an explicitly labelled final page is present. No re-render beyond the cap occurred here.
+4. Locate the actual military/TMU log, or its documented noncreation/search/retention history, and the rules underlying the review's role-specific assertions.
+5. Pursue the separate **actual May 2003 draft/corrected QFR/delivery** and **signed administrative action/no-action/reasons and recommendation-specific implementation/closure**. These newly located 2001 operational forms do not supply those outcomes.
+
+All five tracks and all eighteen substantive criteria remain partial/open. Native telephone joins, recorder configuration/custody/output/clocks, materials specimen/native/calibration/same-specimen joins and steel native preservation/transfer/inventory/attribution/selection inputs remain TODOs. Prior technical tests are neither duplicated nor relabelled unperformed. No outreach, new request, fee, filing, private mailbox/correspondence, private push, deletion, source overwrite or history rewrite occurred.
+
+## Verification and revision accountability
+
+[verify_forms.py](verify_forms.py) and [VERIFICATION.json](VERIFICATION.json) preserve **33 passing scoped checks, zero failures**: whole-source identity/page count, 16 raster identities, six performed-OCR identities/line counts, selected safe typed anchors, three daily-label locators, conditional nominal arithmetic, explicit scope and changed-source controls. Handwriting, role/event joins, blank-grid readings, footer/pagination readings and source representation warnings remain manual observations.
+
+A rerun uses Python 3.12.14 / pypdf 6.10.0:
+
+```sh
+python3 verify_forms.py --pdf /path/to/AEA1130.pdf --media-root /path/to/faa-operational-form-crosswalk-2026-10-30
+```
+
+Passing these checks establishes reproduction of qualified fields, not original-event accuracy, complete custody, native authenticity, clock alignment, compliance, delivery, source independence or intent. Earlier source versions and failed checks remain unchanged.
+
+| Requirement | Outcome | Remaining limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| Inspect underlying referenced forms | Actual 7230-4 and Area B 3600-1/certification counterparts read | Exact native versions, statement period and duty rules unverified |
+| Preserve conflicts and scopes | Earlier claims, both Time Off values and all candidate clock labels kept side by side | No chosen controlling value or resolved explanation |
+| Test feasible fields | Source/derivative identity, typed anchors and conditional arithmetic reproduced | No independent clock/decoder/voice test |
+| Carry unfinished work forward | Pagination, military/TMU, statement/rules and May 2003/2006 originals remain TODOs | No substantive criterion closed |
+| Revision diff | [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff), new additive unit against absent-file baseline | Earlier records unchanged; separate from image reading |
+| Publish as AveLyra | Safe notes, pins, selected operational fields and code/results only | Separate local receipt verifies identity, ref and every remote body; no main merge claimed |
